<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  [XND] Nocturnal Animals (Continued) (Mlie.XNDNocturnalAnimals, Workshop 2269731409, itself a
  continuation of XeoNovaDan.NocturnalAnimals) does not infer an animal's activity cycle from any
  vanilla field: it hand-lists specific vanilla defNames - Hare, Cat, the big cats, several birds
  - and adds its own NocturnalAnimals.ExtendedRaceProperties ModExtension to each by name. Sloth
  is not vanilla and is absent from every one of its patch files, so it is silently unaffected
  whether or not this mod runs, exactly like the trade tag and biome gaps ATTRIBUTION.md already
  documents for the port itself.

  Real sloths are active mostly at night and sleep through most of the day, which is the animal's
  own flavour text in Defs/ThingDefs_Animals.xml ("sleeps most of the day and eats the rest") -
  Nocturnal fits that description better than Crepuscular, which this mod reserves for dawn/dusk
  feeders such as the hare. No balance value changes: this only lets the sloth's already-declared
  sleep pattern show up as an actual daily cycle when this specific mod is present.

  Guarded by PatchOperationFindMod on the mod's display name, so it remains fully optional:
  without it, this file changes nothing and logs nothing. loadAfter is declared in About.xml so
  the mod's assembly - which defines NocturnalAnimals.ExtendedRaceProperties - is present before
  this operation resolves the class.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>[XND] Nocturnal Animals (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Sloth"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="NocturnalAnimals.ExtendedRaceProperties">
          <bodyClock>Nocturnal</bodyClock>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
